    "old_content": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4664,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"lymphasia-educational-image\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large lymphasia-educational-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-consultation-lymphedema-assessment.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun consultation image for lymphedema assessment in Singapore\" class=\"wp-image-4664\"/><figcaption>Specialist consultation focuses on diagnosis, imaging, treatment selection and long-term care planning.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<div class=\"hermes-nassif-elective-pathway-20260927\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9e8e5;border-radius:18px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8fcfb 0%,#eef7f4 100%);padding:20px;margin:24px 0;box-shadow:0 12px 28px rgba(14,58,51,.06)\">\n  <p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2f665e;font-weight:700\">Start here: assessment pathway</p>\n  <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-size:28px;line-height:1.12\">Find the right lymphedema pathway before choosing a treatment</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;color:#304743;line-height:1.65\">Lymphedema care is not a single procedure decision. A useful first step is to clarify the cause and stage of swelling, whether compression or decongestive therapy has been optimised, whether cellulitis has occurred, and whether imaging such as ICG lymphography or ultrasound is needed before surgery is discussed.</p>\n  <div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:12px\">\n    <a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/lymphedema-treatment/\" style=\"display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3eeeb;border-radius:14px;padding:14px;text-decoration:none;color:#153832\"><strong>Treatment overview</strong><br><span style=\"font-size:14px;color:#53635f\">CDT, compression, imaging and surgery options.</span></a>\n    <a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/lva-surgery-singapore/\" style=\"display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3eeeb;border-radius:14px;padding:14px;text-decoration:none;color:#153832\"><strong>LVA / LVB surgery</strong><br><span style=\"font-size:14px;color:#53635f\">Suitability, limits, recovery and alternatives.</span></a>\n    <a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/contact/\" style=\"display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3eeeb;border-radius:14px;padding:14px;text-decoration:none;color:#153832\"><strong>Assessment enquiry</strong><br><span style=\"font-size:14px;color:#53635f\">For non-urgent specialist consultation planning.</span></a>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"margin:14px 0 0;color:#53635f;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55\">LymphedAsia is an educational resource. Online information does not replace personalised consultation, and suitability for surgery varies by individual assessment.</p>\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:image -->",
